# What Vercel must not upload to the backend function bundle.
#
# Measured, not guessed: the backend directory is ~700 MB on disk and
# Vercel's bundle is ~550 MB, which is the whole tree rather than the
# code. The cause is .venv — 207 MB of an interpreter and the packages
# Vercel installs itself anyway from requirements.txt — plus pytest's
# caches and the local database, none of which a serverless function
# needs. Excluding them takes the uploaded set from ~700 MB to the
# application itself, and the deployed function stays far inside the
# size limit.
#
# Keep this list tied to measurement: an entry here that stops being
# large should be removed, and a new large directory (a corpus, a
# fixtures bundle) belongs here the moment it appears.
.venv
venv
env
ENV

# Bytecode caches. They are per-interpreter and wrong on any other.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# The local database and its journals. On the server the database is
# provisioned from SCHOLARZONE_DATABASE_URL; a checked-out copy of the
# dev catalogue would ship 17 MB of rows (and, in the wrong hands, the
# whole directory) inside a bundle.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The test suite runs in CI, not in the function. tests/ imports
# pytest, and its fixtures would otherwise drag the dependency in
# through the import graph even when nothing calls them.
tests/

# Local and editor state that is not the application.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
